# The app menu's "Modern controls" (wish of a user, 12.11.2026, Controls page): the left stick moves Leon in the
# direction it points, as the camera sees it, instead of the original's tank controls. Off (the default): as the game.
# player.cpp re4ModernPrepare runs before the movement routine (pl_R0_Move; only the free-moving routines: idle,
# walk, back step, run, turn): Leon turns toward the stick (at most 0.25 rad a frame) and the routine is told "up"
# (Key bit 1) only, with the back / left / right bits off (restored afterwards), so walk and run start and stop as
# always. The digital pad does the same. The shoulder camera follows Leon's yaw, so a camera-relative stick would
# circle: while Leon walks and stands the camera keeps a yaw of its own (g_re4_modern_cam_yaw, turned by the right
# stick; cam_qfps.cpp calcBaseMatrix builds its base matrix from it), otherwise the yaw follows Leon's. With the
# aim key held Leon first turns to where the camera looks, then the game's aim routine runs unchanged.
# Walking while aiming: in the weapon routine with the aim key held the app sends the move stick as the C stick
# (Key.substick; the aim stick is the main stick), and re4ModernAimWalk moves Leon's position over the ground
# (re4_modern_aim_walk mm a frame at the full stick, the way MotionAddSpeed adds the root motion), the aim pose
# of the game unchanged: he glides, there is no walking animation for the legs.
# Not covered: ladders, crouching, boats, pushing and the knife keep the original keys; the back step and the
# B+down quick turn are off while the switch is on (the stick turns him around instead).
# Bone list: the first time the switch is on, leon_bones.txt in the app's files folder (re4ModernDumpBones).
# Legs while aiming: re4ModernLegs runs Leon's walk motion on a work of its own after the weapon routine and lets only
# the leg parts (17 hip joint, 18-21 left leg, 22-25 right leg, from leon_bones.txt) take its pose; the others are
# skipped for that call (parts flag bit 29), so the aim pose stays. The walk's speed follows the glide's speed.
# The aim bends the pelvis (part 0) with the aim pitch: the hip joint (17) gets the walk's pose turned back by the
# difference of the walk's and the aim pose's pelvis rotations, so the legs keep their direction (not stretched).
# The legs only: the game blends the aim up / down motion into the parts' matrices after its partsMatCalc (matBlend), the angles
# the parts keep are the raw motion's: re4ModernLegs builds the matrices of the leg parts 17..25 itself and leaves the rest as the game has them.
# The legs' IK: the walk motion has the foot target of its leg chains in the effector parts' position (model space) and the knee
# comes from the game's two-bone IK (ik.cpp): re4ModernLegs runs IKInit with the walk motion, the world matrices of the leg parts,
# InverseKinematics and the parts under the legs, then the aim motion's IK set-up and the parts' flags back.
# The bob: while Leon walks aiming the body (the world matrices of all parts and of the weapon) goes up and down by a small step
# (re4_modern_bob mm top to bottom) and sways to the side of the foot on the floor (re4_modern_sway) with the beat of the feet of the last frame; the leg IK keeps the feet on their targets.
# The bob goes into the hips' local matrix too (the game builds the world matrices again from the local ones after this) and the arms
# (the shoulders 5 and 11 with everything under them and the weapon) follow the body with a delay (re4_modern_arm_gain).
# The bob and the arms' delay are applied by re4ModernBodyShift in the LOCAL matrices of the hips (0) and the shoulders (5, 11),
# once a frame: first thing in cPlayer::setLaserSight (pl_class.cpp: the laser is drawn from the weapon there, so it moves with the
# gun), else in re4ModernLegs before the world matrices are built again.
# Two switches, each works without the other: "Modern controls" (re4_modern_controls: the stick moves Leon as the camera sees it, the
# right stick turns the camera) and "Walk while aiming" (re4_modern_aimwalk: the walk with the aim key held, the legs, the bob).
# re4_modern_arm_gain 0: the arms move exactly with the body.
